# Cross-language protocol contract

- Maintain a language-neutral schema source of truth (JSON Schema or Protobuf, chosen in an ADR) and generated/validated TS/Python representations. Current TS types are a bootstrap, not a wire validator.
- Contract changes require compatibility analysis, schema-version increment when breaking, migrations/replay fixtures, and an ADR.
- Define device ID, monotonic sequence, channel-major/sample-major layout, samples per block, physical units, timebase, clock correction, acquisition vs receipt timestamp, dropped sample count and signal quality.
- Never infer sample timestamp solely from render arrival time. Synthetic/test signals must carry provenance.
- Add contract tests for producer and consumer; reject unknown/badly shaped frames in a controlled way.
